[{:seon.task/name "build-smoke-is-green-on-the-pin"
  :seon.task/plan "Jolt's build-smoke.sh fails on our pin 9e42a0d8 at its first check: \"startup profile missing marker: native pre-main (exec+ld)\". A smoke that is red on the pin proves nothing for any Jolt change since. Find whether the marker is missing because of our build (the patched Chez, our launcher) or the test's assumption about its environment, fix it at its cause, and make build-smoke part of what a Jolt pin bump must pass."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "a-deftype-method-call-takes-a-site-cache"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-27 (task datahike.transaction/an-index-insert-allocates-nothing-extra): an interop call of a deftype's declared method, (.lookup s k cmp), (.cons s k cmp), (.root s) on persistent-sorted-set's PersistentSortedSet, costs 60 ticks and 80 B with no work in it, and a PSS lookup with a free comparator ~300 B. Cause: jolt-host-site-call0..3 (reference-code/jolt/host/chez/java/host-static.ss) cache only a jhost receiver; a jrec builds the argument vector, walks method-dispatch-arms (record-method-dispatch) and the dotform arm's cond (dot-forms.ss), whose rest args become a list, before jrec-method-arity finds the method. The fix: the site keeps (desc . method) for a jrec receiver, as jrec-field-site-ref does for a field read, filled only when the dotform arm would itself take the declared method (no user-override arm, not a field read, not a class field with no args, not an IFn or transient method the arm answers first), and calls it with no vector. Proofs: a Jolt chez test of bytes a call (0 past the method's own), and seon.db-test/a-value-costs-its-index-inserts's overrun closing."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.db-test/a-value-costs-its-index-inserts}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-try-entered-allocates-nothing"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-27 (task datahike.transaction/an-index-insert-allocates-nothing-extra): entering a try/catch whose body does not throw costs 176 B on Jolt ((try (compare a b) (catch Exception e 0)) against 0 B for the compare alone), so a library that wraps a hot call in a try pays it per call; Datahike's compare-value and cmp-attr-nil each grew a type test to skip the try (jolt/compare-value-no-try, jolt/attribute-compare-without-try). The try is emitted at its site as a one-shot escape and a hand-pushed handler (Jolt c22cb9c0, 00a3b321, reference-code/jolt/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme.clj); find what of that allocates per entry (the escape continuation, the handler frame, a closure over the body) and make the no-throw path allocate nothing. Once it does, Datahike's two type tests can go. Proof: a Jolt chez test of bytes per try entered (0), and seon.db-test/an-identity-costs-its-seek."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
